WEBVTT

00:06:58.789 --> 00:07:00.416
I'm a scientist,

00:07:00.416 --> 00:07:02.293
I have a doctorate in astrophysics,

00:07:02.334 --> 00:07:04.044
I've published in the top journals,

00:07:04.086 --> 00:07:06.755
in wave-particle interactions,
space physics,

00:07:06.755 --> 00:07:08.883
nucleic acid biochemistry.

00:07:08.883 --> 00:07:11.969
I've actually been trained
to get to the bottom of things, so --

00:07:12.011 --> 00:07:13.095
(Laughter)

00:07:13.137 --> 00:07:14.388
I went online --

00:07:14.430 --> 00:07:18.726
(Applause)

00:07:19.477 --> 00:07:23.314
So I went online, and I found
fascinating research papers.

00:07:23.355 --> 00:07:26.650
I learned that these DNA knot things
are not always bad.

00:07:26.650 --> 00:07:28.986
Actually, the knotting and unknotting --

00:07:29.028 --> 00:07:31.363
it's like a complicated computer language.